# Symbolic view of the /usr/bin/tree entry: every row is one instruction of
# main with its osaca latency. Only the callee-saved prologue pushes are
# pinned as an unordered set (their order moves with the tree build) plus
# one call to anchor the body; frame sizes and canaries move with the build.
# REQUIRES: x86_64, tree
# RUN: perf analyze /usr/bin/tree:main -e index,assembly,latency 2>&1 | %FileCheck %s
# CHECK-NOT: Traceback
# CHECK: index assembly latency
# CHECK-NEXT: endbr64
# CHECK-DAG: push r15 12.00
# CHECK-DAG: push r14 12.00
# CHECK: call
# CHECK-NOT: Traceback
